.* QUIWRKDDMF: WRKDDMF, the DDM files the name selects with their
.* options. Options 5 and 6 are DSPFD of the file, F22 every value whole.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=POSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=LCLCL BASETYPE='CHAR 21'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=RMTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 33'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=LOCCL BASETYPE='CHAR 255'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=POSTO CLASS=POSCL.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=LCLFILE CLASS=LCLCL.
:VAR NAME=RMTFILE CLASS=RMTCL.
:VAR NAME=RMTLOC CLASS=LOCCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=FILES VARS='OPT LCLFILE RMTFILE RMTLOC'.
:KEYL NAME=KEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION='RETURN 9'.F9=Print list
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F22 ACTION='RETURN 22'.F22=Display entire field
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKDDMF KEYL=KEYS HELP=WRKDDMFH ENTER='RETURN 0' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with DDM Files
:DATA DEPTH=2.
:DATACOL WIDTH=24.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAI VAR=POSTO USAGE=INOUT HELP='FLD/POSTO'.Position to
:EDATA.
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=FILES SCROLL=YES MAXHEAD=2.(No DDM files)
:LISTACT OPTION=1 ENTER='CMD ?CRTDDMF' HELP='WRKDDMF/OPTIONS'.1=Create DDM file
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGDDMF FILE(&LCLFILE.)' HELP='WRKDDMF/OPTIONS'.2=Change DDM file
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD DLTF FILE(&LCLFILE.)' HELP='WRKDDMF/OPTIONS'.4=Delete
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD DSPFD FILE(&LCLFILE.)' HELP='WRKDDMF/OPTIONS'.5=Display details
:LISTACT OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD DSPFD FILE(&LCLFILE.) OUTPUT(*PRINT)' HELP='WRKDDMF/OPTIONS'.6=Print details
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKDDMF/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=LCLFILE USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/LCLFILE'.Local File
:LISTCOL VAR=RMTFILE USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=29 HELP='FLD/RMTFILE'.Remote File
:LISTCOL VAR=RMTLOC USAGE=OUTPUT ATCOL=63 MAXWIDTH=14 HELP='FLD/RMTLOC'.Remote Location
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKDDMFH.Work with DDM Files - Help
:P.The DDM files the name selects: for each, the local file a program
opens and the file and system the requests go to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 and F12 leave, F5 reads the files again, F22 shows each remote
file and location whole.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='FLD/POSTO'.Position to
:P.Type the first characters of a local file name to put that file at
the top of the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKDDMF/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LCLFILE'.Local File
:P.The DDM file on this system, with its library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RMTFILE'.Remote File
:P.The file on the remote system the DDM file's requests reach.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RMTLOC'.Remote Location
:P.The system the requests go to: its host name or address, or the
relational database directory entry that names it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKDDMF/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Create DDM file
:PD.Type 1 and press Enter to create a DDM file. The Create DDM File
(CRTDDMF) command is prompted.
:PT.2=Change DDM file
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
DDM File (CHGDDMF) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
File (DLTF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display details
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to see its attributes. The
Display File Description (DSPFD) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Print details
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to print its attributes. The
Display File Description (DSPFD) command prints them for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
